foopgp-hugowebsite for Debian
=============================

This package installs the tooling to serve https://foopgp.org from its Hugo
sources. It does NOT contain the website: the site is a git clone that the
update job bootstraps under /var/www/foopgp-hugowebsite/ on its first run.

What the package installs
-------------------------
  /usr/share/foopgp-hugowebsite/update_hugo.sh   pull sources + `hugo --minify`
  /usr/share/foopgp-hugowebsite/goaccess.sh       access-log stats → public/goaccess/
  /etc/cron.d/foopgp-hugowebsite                  run both as www-data (6 / 5 min)
  /etc/apache2/sites-available/foopgp.conf        the virtual host
  /var/log/foopgp-hugowebsite/                    update_hugo.sh log

Bringing a fresh host online
----------------------------
  sudo apt install foopgp-hugowebsite

  # Serve the virtual host:
  sudo a2ensite foopgp
  sudo service apache2 reload

  # The cron bootstraps the clone within ~6 min. To build immediately:
  sudo -u www-data /usr/share/foopgp-hugowebsite/update_hugo.sh

The update job clones from codeberg (origin) and configures a github mirror
remote; `git pull` always follows origin — the mirrors are never force-pushed.

Out of scope — DNS
------------------
Point the domain at this host. Create A (and AAAA for IPv6) records:

  foopgp.org.        A     <this-host-IPv4>
  www.foopgp.org.    A     <this-host-IPv4>
  foopgp.org.        AAAA  <this-host-IPv6>   # if available
  www.foopgp.org.    AAAA  <this-host-IPv6>

For high availability you may publish several A/AAAA records (DNS round-robin),
or front the hosts with a load balancer / CDN. Verify with:

  dig +short foopgp.org
  getent hosts foopgp.org

Out of scope — HTTPS (Let's Encrypt / certbot)
----------------------------------------------
The shipped vhost is HTTP (:80) only. Once DNS resolves to this host, obtain and
auto-install a certificate — certbot edits the apache config and adds the :443
vhost and the HTTP→HTTPS redirect for you:

  sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-apache
  sudo certbot --apache -d foopgp.org -d www.foopgp.org

Renewal is handled automatically by the certbot systemd timer / cron; test it:

  sudo certbot renew --dry-run

(The -d list must match the vhost's ServerName + ServerAlias, i.e. both
foopgp.org and www.foopgp.org.)
